  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promoting basic literacy skills in primary education in Mexico</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In recent assesments, Mexico has shown that primary education students do not have the necessary language skills, with school closure due to the Covid 19 pandemic, this issue has deepened. The office has been working with vulnerable populations to ensure development of literacy basic skills and competencies. In addition, we will be working specifically with migrants in coordination with San Jose an Guatemala offices to ensure a strategy for education of migrants that is contextualized to the specific challenges in this region. Finally, we are working in the response to the Hurricane in Guerrero that impacted at least 600 schools last november.</narrative>
  </description>
